{
  "about": "Steven Piano's built-in playlists (DESIGN.md > v1.5 - M17). Lists in their order; each piece is a matcher: composer = the library's composerKey (the folded surname ComposerNames gives; a list allows arrangers, and \"\" is an unknown composer), title = a case-insensitive regular expression found in the folded title (TextKeys.fold), collection = the INDEX.csv collection, exactly, when given. A matcher adds at most four pieces, by folded title; a piece appears once. Popular and Recognisable skip MAESTRO's numbered repeats (\"... [2]\"). Epic on piano matches each piece of the Epic zip under the three names the same file can have: the zip's, a folder import's (INDEX.csv) and ALL-SONGS.zip's. Only what the library holds is ever listed: public-domain and openly licensed files.",
